invariant: INV-48
file: src/mldsa.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh mldsa-vector
reason: the verifier samples A on the four-way Keccak where the session's
  ch_cfg.cpu holds CH_CPU_VAES, not CH_CPU_AVX2, so a value with AVX2 and
  without VAES samples A on sha3.c, and one with VAES alone runs AVX2 on a
  CPU the caller did not say has it. Every verdict stays right, so
  bin/mldsa_runtime_test counts the calls into the sampler under every
  value. Only an x86-64 compiler reads the line, so the script builds the
  binary for x86-64 and runs it under qemu-x86_64. The lane skips without
  docker, and this then reports unguarded rather than caught.

--- old
    if (mld_wide_runs(cpu)) {
        return mld_row_sum_wide(cpu, sum, room, i, pk, z_hat);
--- new
    if (cpu & CH_CPU_VAES) {
        return mld_row_sum_wide(cpu, sum, room, i, pk, z_hat);
